    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe app now supports an optional `postcode` on owners, validated per the fixed region table.\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (not in `required`), with `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$` and length 4. Because it lives on `OwnerFields`, it flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto` via `allOf`), and the bean-validation constraint rejects a malformed value like `\"12\"` with a 400 at the request edge.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `postcode` field with getter/setter and `@Column(name = \"postcode\")`. MapStruct auto-maps it on the way in and out, so it's stored and returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`PostcodeValidator.java`** (new util) \u2014 Resolves the city's region via the existing `LocalityResolver`, then checks the postcode against the inclusive range for that region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). A `null` postcode is skipped (optional), an unknown-region city accepts any 4-digit value, and an out-of-range value throws `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n\n4. **`InvalidPostcodeException.java`** (new) \u2014 Subclass of `InvalidOwnerFieldException`, so the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` handler maps it to a 400 with no new handler needed.\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Calls `PostcodeValidator.validate(city, postcode)` in the create normalization step.\n\n6. **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added a `postcode` column so the field persists across all supported databases.\n\nThe request contract stays backward-compatible: an owner created without a postcode is still accepted, matching the spec and the `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode` test.\n\nOne note on scope: the spec is phrased around owner *creation* (\"an owner created without a postcode\u2026\"), and the tests only exercise `POST /api/owners`, so I wired validation into the create path only. `updateOwner` doesn't currently read or validate `postcode` \u2014 say the word if you'd like the update path to handle it too.",
